==English==
[[File:Pierogi.jpg|thumb|A plate of '''pierogies'''.]]

===Alternative forms===
* [[pirogi]], [[perogie]], [[perogi]], [[pyrogy]], [[pyrohy]], [[perogy]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|pl|en}} {{term|pierogi||lang=pl}}, singular {{term|pieróg||lang=pl}}, or {{etyl|uk|en}} {{term|пироги||tr=pyrohý|lang=uk|sc=Cyrl}}, {{singular}} {{term|пиріг||tr=pyríh|lang=uk|sc=Cyrl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/pəˈroːɡi/}}
* {{hyphenation|pier|ogi|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pierogi|pierogies|pierogis}}

# {{context|North America|lang=en}} A [[square]]- or [[crescent]]-shaped [[dumpling]] of [[unleavened]] [[dough]], [[stuff]]ed with [[sauerkraut]], [[cheese]], [[mash]]ed [[potatoes]], [[cabbage]], [[onion]], [[meat]], or any combination of these, or with a [[fruit]] [[filling]].

====Synonyms====
* [[varenyky]]/[[vareniki]] {{qualifier|plural}}
* [[pelmeni]] {{qualifier|plural}}
* [[pedahey]]

====Derived terms====
* [[Chinese perogy]]

